te, image, drive, WP)\n   Impact: Each exec = new bash process, Python interpreter load, file I/O\n\n2. REDUNDANT verify_artifacts.py CALLS\n   Current: 5 calls per story (pre_write, pre_sync, post_sync, pre_drive, pre_wp)\n   Each validates the same manifest repeatedly\n   Impact: 5 Python processes, redundant JSON parsing, file reads\n\n3. ENVIRONMENT RE-SOURCING\n   Current: 'source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh' in EVERY exec block\n   Count: 20+ times in this run\n   Impact: Bash overhead, redundant variable assignment\n\n4. PICKER OVERHEAD FOR FEED_DRAIN\n   Current: Picker spawned for classify-only mode (no selection logic)\n   - N=1 in feed drain = only 1 candidate, no diversity needed\n   - Picker adds 18s runtime\n   Impact: Unnecessary spawn when human already selected the story\n\n5. MULTI-PART EXEC BLOCKS\n   Current: Sequential script calls in separate exec\n   Example: validate + update_recent_topics + update_manifest = 3 exec\n   Could be: 1 Python script doing all 3, or chained with &&\n\n6. TOKEN AGGREGATION OVERHEAD\n   Current: aggregate_run_tokens.py reads all agent outputs at end\n   Could be: Agents write tokens to manifest incrementally","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1785238392243}}
{"type":"message","id":"46abf654","parentId":"02143d2c","timestamp":"2026-07-28T11:33:31.439Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a21670806e883a65","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat <<'EOF'\n=== DETAILED RECOMMENDATIONS ===\n\n## 1. BATCH MANIFEST UPDATES\n\n**Problem:** \n- update_manifest_step.sh called 5x per story\n- Each spawns bash + Python + JSON read/write\n- Separate update_pick_status.py calls (4x per story)\n\n**Solution A: Merge Step Updates**\nCreate a single `advance_pipeline_step.py` that handles:\n- Manifest step update\n- Pick status update\n- Timestamps\n- One atomic write\n\n```python\n# advance_pipeline_step.py\ndef advance_step(manifest, step, pick_id=None, pick_status=None):\n    m = json.load(manifest)\n    m[\"steps\"][step] = {\"status\": \"succeeded\", \"ts\": now()}\n    if pick_status:\n        update_pick_in_db(pick_id, pick_status, ...)\n    json.dump(m, manifest)\n```\n\n**Impact:** Reduces 5 exec calls → 1 per story\n**Time Saved:** ~2-3 seconds per story\n\n---\n\n## 2. ELIMINATE REDUNDANT verify_artifacts CALLS\n\n**Problem:**\n- verify_artifacts.py called 5x: pre_write, pre_sync, post_sync, pre_drive, pre_wp\n- Most checks are redundant (file exists, manifest fields)\n- Total overhead: ~5 seconds per story\n\n**Solution:**\n\n**Option A: Inline Critical Checks**\nOnly verify what matters at each transition:\n- Pre-write: research file exists (already validated)\n- Pre-sync: raw.md exists (writer just wrote it)\n- Pre-drive: final.md + image exist (artifact gates)\n- Pre-WP: wordpress.json not needed (publish.sh validates)\n\n**Option B: Lazy Verification**\nOnly verify on ERROR, not on every step.\nTrust the previous agent's success.\n\n**Option C: Batch Verification**\nOne script that runs ALL artifact checks in a single Python process:\n```bash\npython3 verify_all_artifacts.py --stages pre_write,pre_sync,post_sync,pre_drive,pre_wp\n```\n\n**Impact:** 5 calls → 1 call (or 0 if trusting agent success)\n**Time Saved:** ~5 seconds per story\n\n---\n\n## 3. PERSIST ENVIRONMENT IN ORCHESTRATOR CONTEXT\n\n**Problem:**\n- `source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh` in EVERY exec block\n- 20+ times in this run\n- Each source is fast but adds up\n\n**Solution:**\nKeep critical vars in orchestrator's working memory:\n- RUN_DIR, PIPELINE_MANIFEST, PROJECT_SLUG, GROUP_CHAT_ID\n- Pass as args to scripts, don't rely on re-sourcing\n\n**Already doing this partially** (passed paths in spawn messages)\n\n**Impact:** Marginal (0.5s), but cleaner code\n\n---\n\n## 4. SKIP PICKER FOR FEED_DRAIN (N=1)\n\n**Problem:**\n- FEED_DRAIN = human already selected ONE story\n- Picker in classify-only mode just labels categories\n- But picker adds 18s runtime + token cost\n- For N=1 with 1 candidate, no diversity logic needed\n\n**Solution A: Fast-path FEED_DRAIN with N=1**\nWhen FEED_DRAIN + N=1 + 1 candidate:\n```bash\n# Skip picker, directly inject:\npython3 inject_single_pick.py --pick-id $PICK_ID \\\n  --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" --wp-categories-from-pool\n```\n\n**Solution B: Inline Category Assignment**\nbuild_picker_input.py already injects wp_category_ids\nJust write those directly to picks.json without picker spawn\n\n**Impact:** Saves 18 seconds on every FEED_DRAIN story\n**Time Saved:** ~15-20s per auto-published story\n\n---\n\n## 5. CHAIN SEQUENTIAL SCRIPTS\n\n**Problem:**\n- validate_research.py\n- check_recent_topic_duplicates.py\n- update_recent_topics.py\n- verify_artifacts.py pre_write\n- All separate exec calls (4 exec)\n\n**Solution:**\nCombine into single `post_research_pipeline.py`:\n```bash\npython3 post_research_pipeline.py \\\n  --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" \\\n  --picks \"$RUN_DIR/picker/picks.json\" \\\n  --pick-index $PICK_INDEX \\\n  --run-id \"$RUN_ID-iter$PICK_INDEX\"\n```\n\nThis script does:\n1. Validate research\n2. Check topic duplicates\n3. Update registry\n4. Verify artifacts\n5. Return single PASS/FAIL\n\n**Impact:** 4 exec → 1 exec\n**Time Saved:** ~3-4 seconds per story\n\n---\n\n## 6. EMBED TOKEN TRACKING IN AGENT SUCCESS\n\n**Problem:**\n- aggregate_run_tokens.py runs at end, re-reads all agent outputs\n- Could be incremental\n\n**Solution:**\nEach agent's success callback writes tokens to manifest:\n```json\n{\n  \"steps\": {\n    \"research\": {\n      \"tokens_in\": 1234,\n      \"tokens_out\": 567,\n      \"model\": \"qwen.qwen3-coder-next\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nOrchestrator reads from manifest, no separate aggregation.\n\n**Impact:** 1 less script at end, cleaner token tracking\n**Time Saved:** ~1 second\n\n---\n\n## 7. REDUCE ORCHESTRATOR THINKING OVERHEAD\n\n**Current:** \n- Large `<thinking>` blocks before every step\n- Verbose status updates\n\n**Optimization:**\n- Brief thinking blocks (1-2 lines)\n- Trust the SOUL.md to encode the procedure\n- Only think when deviation/ambiguity occurs\n\n**Impact:** Faster response generation, fewer tokens\n\n---\n\n## 8. PARALLELIZE INDEPENDENT WORK\n\n**Current:** Sequential execution\n- Picker → Research → Write → Image → Drive → WP\n- Total: 8 minutes\n\n**Potential Parallelization:**\n- Image prompt generation could START during writer execution\n- If writer is at 80% done, creator can begin crafting prompt\n\n**Challenge:** Sequential dependency (image needs headline)\n**Benefit:** May save 30-60s per story\n\n---\n\n## 9. CACHE PROJECT CONFIG LOOKUPS\n\n**Problem:**\n- project_config.py called 5+ times per story\n- Same fields (drive_parent, drive_account, telegram.group_id)\n\n**Solution:**\ninit_run.sh reads ALL fields ONCE and exports them:\n```bash\n# init_run.sh writes to env file:\nexport DRIVE_PREFIX=\"Crypto News\"\nexport DRIVE_PARENT=\"1DiEijL14zMSnuIqycvdoxAIjOgRvxCDx\"\nexport DRIVE_ACCOUNT=\"bhardwaj0sawan@gmail.com\"\nexport GROUP_CHAT_ID=\"-1003760909509\"\nexport TEMPLATE_PATH=\"...\"\n```\n\nNever re-query project_config.py mid-run.\n\n**Impact:** Eliminates 5 Python calls per story\n**Time Saved:** ~2-3 seconds\n\n---\n\n## 10. MERGE SYMLINK CLEANUP INTO INIT\n\n**Problem:**\n- 12 symlinks created at start\n- 12 symlinks removed at end (cleanup_run_artifacts.sh)\n- Legacy artifact from single-run world\n\n**Solution:**\n- Use hashed run directories (already doing this)\n- Remove symlink creation entirely\n- Or keep only debug symlinks, skip cleanup script\n\n**Impact:** Simplify code, remove legacy cruft\n\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785238392245,"responseId":"chatcmpl-a89c4a57-8744-4132-9e50-a9ff6853981d"}}
{"type":"message","id":"0546048f","parentId":"46abf654","timestamp":"2026-07-28T11:33:31.833Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a21670806e883a65","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== DETAILED RECOMMENDATIONS ===\n\n## 1. BATCH MANIFEST UPDATES\n\n**Problem:** \n- update_manifest_step.sh called 5x per story\n- Each spawns bash + Python + JSON read/write\n- Separate update_pick_status.py calls (4x per story)\n\n**Solution A: Merge Step Updates**\nCreate a single `advance_pipeline_step.py` that handles:\n- Manifest step update\n- Pick status update\n- Timestamps\n- One atomic write\n\n```python\n# advance_pipeline_step.py\ndef advance_step(manifest, step, pick_id=None, pick_status=None):\n    m = json.load(manifest)\n    m[\"steps\"][step] = {\"status\": \"succeeded\", \"ts\": now()}\n    if pick_status:\n        update_pick_in_db(pick_id, pick_status, ...)\n    json.dump(m, manifest)\n```\n\n**Impact:** Reduces 5 exec calls → 1 per story\n**Time Saved:** ~2-3 seconds per story\n\n---\n\n## 2. ELIMINATE REDUNDANT verify_artifacts CALLS\n\n**Problem:**\n- verify_artifacts.py called 5x: pre_write, pre_sync, post_sync, pre_drive, pre_wp\n- Most checks are redundant (file exists, manifest fields)\n- Total overhead: ~5 seconds per story\n\n**Solution:**\n\n**Option A: Inline Critical Checks**\nOnly verify what matters at each transition:\n- Pre-write: research file exists (already validated)\n- Pre-sync: raw.md exists (writer just wrote it)\n- Pre-drive: final.md + image exist (artifact gates)\n- Pre-WP: wordpress.json not needed (publish.sh validates)\n\n**Option B: Lazy Verification**\nOnly verify on ERROR, not on every step.\nTrust the previous agent's success.\n\n**Option C: Batch Verification**\nOne script that runs ALL artifact checks in a single Python process:\n```bash\npython3 verify_all_artifacts.py --stages pre_write,pre_sync,post_sync,pre_drive,pre_wp\n```\n\n**Impact:** 5 calls → 1 call (or 0 if trusting agent success)\n**Time Saved:** ~5 seconds per story\n\n---\n\n## 3. PERSIST ENVIRONMENT IN ORCHESTRATOR CONTEXT\n\n**Problem:**\n- `source /tmp/coinography-run-env.sh` in EVERY exec block\n- 20+ times in this run\n- Each source is fast but adds up\n\n**Solution:**\nKeep critical vars in orchestrator's working memory:\n- RUN_DIR, PIPELINE_MANIFEST, PROJECT_SLUG, GROUP_CHAT_ID\n- Pass as args to scripts, don't rely on re-sourcing\n\n**Already doing this partially** (passed paths in spawn messages)\n\n**Impact:** Marginal (0.5s), but cleaner code\n\n---\n\n## 4. SKIP PICKER FOR FEED_DRAIN (N=1)\n\n**Problem:**\n- FEED_DRAIN = human already selected ONE story\n- Picker in classify-only mode just labels categories\n- But picker adds 18s runtime + token cost\n- For N=1 with 1 candidate, no diversity logic needed\n\n**Solution A: Fast-path FEED_DRAIN with N=1**\nWhen FEED_DRAIN + N=1 + 1 candidate:\n```bash\n# Skip picker, directly inject:\npython3 inject_single_pick.py --pick-id $PICK_ID \\\n  --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" --wp-categories-from-pool\n```\n\n**Solution B: Inline Category Assignment**\nbuild_picker_input.py already injects wp_category_ids\nJust write those directly to picks.json without picker spawn\n\n**Impact:** Saves 18 seconds on every FEED_DRAIN story\n**Time Saved:** ~15-20s per auto-published story\n\n---\n\n## 5. CHAIN SEQUENTIAL SCRIPTS\n\n**Problem:**\n- validate_research.py\n- check_recent_topic_duplicates.py\n- update_recent_topics.py\n- verify_artifacts.py pre_write\n- All separate exec calls (4 exec)\n\n**Solution:**\nCombine into single `post_research_pipeline.py`:\n```bash\npython3 post_research_pipeline.py \\\n  --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" \\\n  --picks \"$RUN_DIR/picker/picks.json\" \\\n  --pick-index $PICK_INDEX \\\n  --run-id \"$RUN_ID-iter$PICK_INDEX\"\n```\n\nThis script does:\n1. Validate research\n2. Check topic duplicates\n3. Update registry\n4. Verify artifacts\n5. Return single PASS/FAIL\n\n**Impact:** 4 exec → 1 exec\n**Time Saved: