{"type":"message","id":"21399e5b","parentId":"2ac24ea8","timestamp":"2026-07-28T11:42:38.776Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95764387c94333f9","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat <<'EOF'\n=== TOP 3 TURN-REDUCTION RECOMMENDATIONS ===\n\n## Goal: Reduce 45 turns → <7 turns (maintaining 100% safety)\n\n---\n\n## Recommendation 1: Skip Picker for FEED_DRAIN N=1 (+0 savings, but 18 seconds)\n\n**Current problem:**\n- FEED_DRAIN runs picker in classify-only mode\n- Single story already selected by human\n- Picker spawns for 18s just to label categories\n\n**Solution:**\nIn `build_picker_input.py`, detect FEED_DRAIN + N=1 + 1 candidate and write picks.json directly:\n\n```python\n# build_picker_input.py\nif args.feed_job_id and target_count == 1 and len(candidates) == 1:\n    # Fast path: bypass picker entirely\n    write_picks_directly(candidates[0], output_file)\n    print(\"PICK_BYPASS: 1 candidate, wrote picks.json directly\")\n    return\n```\n\n**Turns saved:** 0 (picker still spawned in current structure)\n**Time saved:** 18 seconds per FEED_DRAIN story\n**Safety impact:** None — human already selected the story\n\n---\n\n## Recommendation 2: Compound Post-Agent Validation Scripts (+12 turns)\n\n**Current problem:**\n- validate_research.py (1 turn)\n- check_recent_topic_duplicates.py (1 turn)\n- update_recent_topics.py (1 turn)\n- verify_artifacts.py (1 turn)\n- update_manifest_step.sh (1 turn)\n- update_pick_status.py (1 turn)\n= **6 exec turns per agent completion**\n\n**Solution:**\nCreate 3 compound scripts:\n\n### `post_research_pipeline.py` (combines 5 turns → 1)\n```python\ndef main():\n    validate_research(manifest, picks, pick_index)\n    check_topic_duplicates(validated_json, registry)\n    update_recent_topics(validated_json, registry, run_id, \"researched\")\n    verify_artifacts(manifest, \"pre_write\")\n    update_manifest(manifest, \"research\", \"succeeded\")\n    update_pick_status(pick_id, \"writing\")\n    print(\"POST_RESEARCH_PASS\")\n```\n\n### `post_write_pipeline.py` (combines 5 turns → 1)\n```python\ndef main():\n    verify_artifacts(manifest, \"pre_sync\")\n    sync_article(manifest)\n    autofix_article(article_path)\n    check_article(article_path, research_path)\n    verify_artifacts(manifest, \"post_sync\")\n    update_manifest(manifest, \"write\", \"succeeded\")\n    print(\"POST_WRITE_PASS\")\n```\n\n### `post_wp_pipeline.py` (combines 6 turns → 1)\n```python\ndef main():\n    update_recent_topics(validated_json, registry, run_id, \"drafted\", wp_url)\n    aggregate_tokens(manifest)\n    send_card(manifest, build_token_args())\n    update_pick_status(pick_id, \"published\", tokens)\n    archive_iteration(manifest, pick_index)\n    print(\"POST_WP_PASS\")\n```\n\n**Total turns saved:** 6 + 5 + 6 = **17 turns**\n**New exec turns:** 3 (one per agent completion)\n\n**Safety:**\n- Each compound script exits on first error\n- All intermediate outputs logged\n- Same validation logic, just in one process\n\n---\n\n## Recommendation 3: Chain Sequential Setup Commands (+4 turns)\n\n**Current problem:**\n- Turn 1: claim feed job\n- Turn 2: init_run.sh\n- Turn 3: persist batch metadata\n- Turn 4: build_picker_input.py\n\n= **4 exec turns for setup**\n\n**Solution:**\nChain them in a single compound command:\n\n```bash\n# Single turn: setup + claim + build\nPROJECT_SLUG=\"coinography\"\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator/skills/pipeline/init_run.sh \"$PROJECT_SLUG\" && \\\nsource /tmp/${PROJECT_SLUG}-run-env.sh && \\\npython3 -c \"\nimport editorial_db as db, json, sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.../skills/pipeline')\njob = db.claim_next_feed_job('$PROJECT_SLUG')\nprint(json.dumps({'job_id': job.id, 'feed_id': job.feed_id, 'selection_file': job.selection_file}))\nif not job:\n    print('NO_JOB')\n    sys.exit(1)\n\" | tee /tmp/feed_job.json && \\\npython3 update_manifest_batch.py --manifest \"$PIPELINE_MANIFEST\" --target 1 && \\\npython3 build_picker_input.py --feed-job-id $(jq -r .job_id /tmp/feed_job.json) --classify-only \\\n  --output \"$RUN_DIR/picker/picker_input.json\" --project \"$PROJECT_SLUG\"\n```\n\n**Turns saved:** 4 → 1 (3 turns)\n**Safety:** Exit on any failure (&& chains)\n\n---\n\n## TOTAL TURN REDUCTION\n\n| Optimization | Turns Saved | New Turns | Safety Impact |\n|--------------|-------------|-----------|----------------|\n| 1. Skip picker (time only) | 0 exec turns | Same | None |\n| 2. Compound validation scripts | 17 | 3 | None (same logic) |\n| 3. Chain setup commands | 3 | 1 | None |\n| **TOTAL** | **20** | - | - |\n\n---\n\n## FINAL TURN COUNT AFTER ALL OPTIMIZATIONS\n\n| Stage | Current | Optimized |\n|-------|---------|-----------|\n| Setup + claim | 4 turns | 1 turn |\n| Picker spawn + yield | 3 turns | 3 turns |\n| Post-picker validation | 6 turns | 1 turn |\n| Researcher spawn + yield | 3 turns | 3 turns |\n| Post-research validation | 5 turns | 1 turn |\n| Writer spawn + yield | 3 turns | 3 turns |\n| Post-write validation | 5 turns | 1 turn |\n| Creator spawn + yield | 3 turns | 3 turns |\n| Post-creator validation | 4 turns | 1 turn |\n| Drive upload | 4 turns | 1 turn |\n| WP publish + post-WP | 7 turns | 1 turn |\n| Cleanup + finalize | 3 turns | 1 turn |\n| **TOTAL** | **45 turns** | **17 turns** |\n\n**Reduction: 28 turns (62%)**\n\n---\n\n## Path to <7 Turns\n\nTo reach **under 7 turns**, we need even more aggressive batching:\n\n1. **Combine all spawn/yield into single turn** (currently 4 spawn + 4 yield = 8 turns)\n   - Not possible with current architecture (agents are async)\n   - Would require synchronous agent calls (blocking)\n\n2. **Parallel agent spawns** (would require architecture change)\n   - Spawn researcher + creator in parallel\n   - Would violate dependency (writer needs research)\n\n3. **Pre-computed picks** (for FEED_DRAIN)\n   - Already selected by human, no picker needed\n   - With picker bypass: **saves 18s, not turns**\n\n**Achievable target with current architecture: ~17 turns**\n\nTo reach <7 turns, we'd need fundamental changes:\n- Synchronous agent execution (no yields)\n- Parallel agent spawning where dependencies allow\n- Single compound script for entire pipeline\n\n---\n\n## Practical Recommendation\n\n**Implement Recommendations 1-3 immediately:**\n- 17 turns is practical and safe\n- Each compound script is testable in isolation\n- No architecture changes required\n\n**Long-term (if needed):**\n- Investigate synchronous agent execution mode\n- Allow multiple parallel sessions_spawn (research + creator)\n- Reduce spawn/yield overhead from 8 turns → 4 turns\n\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785238916563,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7dbadf9f-8e79-4904-b343-8ad0339bd6d7"}}
